    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1589">

                <pb facs="1006" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/77.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi><anchor n="153" xml:id="d1589-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-19T10:30:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1914, 10.30 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carranza says you may inform his excellency, the German Ambassador, that General
                    Obregon has received strict orders to give ample protection to all foreigners
                    and their property during and after the coming attack on Guadalajara.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carothers</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1589-f1" n="153" type="source" xml:id="d1589-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the German Ambassador June 20, 1914.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
